 To find \(\frac{25}{3} \cdot \frac{27}{300}\), we can first simplify the expression. <endthink>  
\begin{align*}
\frac{25}{3} \cdot \frac{27}{300} &= \frac{25 \cdot 27}{3 \cdot 300} \\
&= \frac{675}{900}.
\end{align*}  
Next, we can simplify the fraction \(\frac{675}{900}\) by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 675 and 900. The GCD of 675 and 900 is 225. Dividing both the numerator and the denominator by 225, we get:  
\begin{align*}
\frac{675 \div 225}{900 \div 225} &= \frac{3}{4}.
\end{align*}  
Thus, the final answer is \(\boxed{\frac{3}{4}}\).

